# Workstream index

Status: ACTIVE_NAVIGATION
Milestone: Repository-local development and GitHub tracking adoption
Dependencies: None

## Purpose
Navigate actual bounded workstreams while preserving the original lowercase `todo`
directory and its historical records. This index is not itself a workstream.

## Tasks
- Use the numbered files below as reviewed public-safe projections.
- Keep each file's stable identity, issue backlink and eight required fields.
- Synchronize only explicitly allowlisted workstreams.

## Acceptance criteria
- One actual workstream maps to one repository issue and one issue-backed Project item.
- Evidence, target qualification, human acceptance and publication remain separate.

## Completion evidence
Original adoption is technically complete and independently reconciled: ten issues,
ten issue-backed Project items and ten persistent backlinks. Eight are
CLOSED/COMPLETED in Done; two original qualification gaps remain OPEN/In review.
No blocked, conflicting or partial items remain.
Canonical configuration: `.github/todo-sync.json`.
Project: https://github.com/users/Zanark/projects/10 (private owner Project).
Repository issues and these numbered projections are public.
Desktop and release workstreams were subsequently added as lea-11 and lea-12;
their implementation, qualification and publication evidence is recorded separately.
The portable v0.2.0 release is published, downloaded, integrity-verified and
installed; its normal native startup and bundled offline commands passed.
The subsequent lea-13 handoff reuses an existing configured workspace through
ignored private inputs and launch helpers, without exporting authentication or
qualifying a new live run.
The subsequent lea-14 tutorial is locally implemented and technically qualified.
Its read-only source entry covers the desktop controls without starting
automation; the already-published v0.2.0 package is unchanged.
The separate lea-15 follow-through packages that tutorial as Windows v0.2.1.
Exact-source qualification, hosted publication and downloaded/native delivery
must complete before that release workstream is marked DONE.

